Z||000005||BlackStang95||11-09-2001||07:10 PM||||I think selling it could have merit,you got it so cheap you could make money off it, and theres many newer and nicer (and less tempting to drive crazily) cars out there, and moneys not really an object to you.  The fieros main appeal no doubt is its handling, and since youre not gonna want to push it through curves anymore its basically a mid engined miata (not an insult by any means, the newer miats get 8's and 7's 0-60.    ||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnF||11-09-2001||07:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by blazin':<BR><B>Thats not fair!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Fair" has nothing to do with it!<P>As PHIL said "Their house - their rules!"<P>As a 19 y.o. it's time to make up YOUR mind what is important.  This forum has nothing to say about that decision.  You know the rules where you are.  You decide if that is what you want to live by.  If so, fine!  If not, fine!<P>Welcome to the grown-up world!<P>||||reg||11
Z||000007||kempo||11-09-2001||07:25 PM||||Spektrum, man I am sorry to hear that.  It really isn't fair, but neither is life.  As already said, "Their house, their rules."  I know how it can turn out to be hellish when you're also on bad terms with your parents, and chances are you'll never be able to get them to see things your way.  All in all, best of luck!  <BR>If you decide to sell, drop me a line.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000008||Shaun41178||11-09-2001||09:30 PM||||Tell your parents that you have put it up for sale.  <P>Just don't tell them that you are asking $120k for it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  By telling them that you have it up for sale should keep them off your back for awhile.<P>But like the others said, welcome to the adult world.  Time to make adult decisions.  Hope all works out for you.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Spektrum-87GT||11-09-2001||10:09 PM||||the fiero isnt going. I'm not going to sell it. I've decided I'll move out before giving it up. My plan is to take it off the road and do the restoration/modifications i had planned for it all along. It really shouldnt even be on the road right now, if my jeep didnt have impossible to break bolts, my fieros body panels would be in a shop somewhere being painted right now.<P>I've learned a very important lesson from this whole accident. Pushing the limits on public roads is very dangerous, expensive, and is not worth the headaches. In the future I will remember this and not attempt stupid stunts like this. I'm 19... live and learn. I'm just glad this lesson didnt cost me my car, jail time, or someones life. I'm actually starting to be thankful that this is all that happened and I can learn from it, because it could have been a WHOLE lot worse. If you drive like I've been driving for the past 2 months... its inevitable, you're going to get in some kind of accident. Now that I have learned that its not a good idea to act like an indy car driver on the street, I feel a few days older and a few days smarter than I was on wednesday. So to wrap things up, my days of acting like mario andretti around town are over, but my fiero days are far from over.<P>------------------<BR>restoration/modification on hold until who knows when<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/spektrum_87gt/" TARGET=_blank>87 Fiero GT</A><BR>1991 Jeep Cherokee<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.com/bspracklin1/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||fieroX||11-09-2001||10:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B> my days of acting like mario andretti around town are over<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Lord knows mine aren't.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||artherd||11-10-2001||12:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B> So to wrap things up, my days of acting like mario andretti around town are over, but my fiero days are far from over.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, save that for the track  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> (not that I always obey my own advice...  but yeah, open rodes have kittens in boxes and ice and gravel and water and all kinds of nasty shizite  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Do what I did, take an accident, and use it as an excuse to build the car up really nice! (I got coilovers and 17s  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>If money's no object to you, we're talking suspension, 13" Held Motorsports brakes, and maybe an engine swap!  (make sure you do them in that order, racecar boy ~ <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Good for you man  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000012||DRH||11-10-2001||12:54 AM||||Spektrum,<P>I don't know all the reasons your parents want you to get rid of it, but I suspect NOT wanting to attend your funeral is the main one. If you are serious about what you said in your last post, you need to say it to your parents. Do it calmly and sincerely and they may change their mind.<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000013||BlackStang95||11-10-2001||02:18 AM||||restoration/mods?  so you're gonna do an engine swap?  That'll really keep you from driving fast...<P>Not to mention it'll be even harder to do financially if you get tossed out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||rogergarrison||11-10-2001||04:19 AM||||im a lot older than you, but I cant see how they think selling your car to get a different one is going to make you safer. Your mental state shouldnt have anything to do with the car you drive. If you drive like an idiot, your going to do it with a Camaro or a Honda too. Look at all the crazy drivers in SUVs and pickups. There not exactly what Id call road hugging, sports vehicles. You apparently just needed to grow up a little, and like I said trading cars wont do it. All my opinions of course, and by the way I think all guys should be out on their own by 19 anyway. You cant learn responsibity living with mommy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||Back On Holiday||11-10-2001||08:09 AM||||Heres a good plan for ya.<P>i'm not saying going behind your parents back<BR>is the right thing to do, but this SHOULD work out.<P>1st.  get yourself a Post office box.<BR>2nd.  Like a previous post stated, get a<BR>      storage place, use your PO box as <BR>      your mailing address - PREPAY until<BR>      March.<BR>3rd.  goto the local auto tags place and<BR>      get a new lisc plate(make sure if they<BR>      have to send away to the DMV that they<BR>      either send it to your PO box or you<BR>      Pickup from the location) If you have <BR>      to, explain that under any  <BR>      circumstances that your parents must<BR>      not know!<BR>4th.  change any distinguishing marks that<BR>      your Fiero has that can be easily<BR>      identifyed by your parents.<BR>5th.  When March comes, get a new paint job<BR>      and with your new plates and your<BR>      interior/exterior looking diffrent or<BR>      bone stock.<P>Now here comes the REAL hard part, deciding what to do, you could tell the truth hoping that your parents have cooled down and maybe<BR>they're not going to kick you out, or you could lay down a REAL wopper and tell them<BR>a real good lie...tell them that you<BR>bought this car for $150 from a fellow fiero owner who needed the $ that day for his morgage or he'd lose his house.<P>Now thats upto you, just pointing out your options.  If I was in your place, i'd do the first 5 steps, then when springtime came I would probably tell them and say' hey, what could I do that will allow you to trust me driving this car?<BR><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||1
Z||000016||tomanyfieros||11-10-2001||10:11 AM||||u can store it at my house for free! i loved to wake up every morning and see someones fiero GT atmy house.... if u want, u can! if not, i may trade another fiero to u for it! that way u can stay in the fieros! LMK! THanx JAson<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
Z||000017||FieroKyle||11-10-2001||10:13 AM||||Yeah, true. I think going 90 in a honda or 120 in a Fiero will kill most people anyway. Doesn't matter on the car, just the driver. Every car goes fast (if ya wait long enough and have enough highway!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).<P>Anyways, just clean up your act and make a point to your parents.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000018||cadero2dmax||11-10-2001||11:04 AM||||Don't give up driving hard - just do it in an organized motorsport.<P>Try autocrossing. This is a cheap way to get involved, and I guarantee that it will make you a more aware and better driver.<P>As far as your parents go, I would almost be willing to bet that there is more of a background here than we are hearing (and that is OK too). I simply feel it is nobody's place to offer the kind of advice you seek without "the rest of the story". So either you give all the facts, or don't seek any advice.<P>G||||reg||1
