Z||000031||Raydar||11-11-2001||12:50 PM||||I would go with the Celica over the Cougar.<BR>Say what you will about Toyotas. They're pretty much as reliable as an anvil.<BR>I think the Cougar has a lot of the same underpinnings as a &lt;cough&gt; Probe. <BR>Unless it just comes down to the point that you've <I>gotta</I> have the Cougar.<BR>I think Mustangs are kinda cool, too. Is a GT out of the question?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000032||FieroKyle||11-11-2001||03:39 PM||||You guys say a Cougar looks nice then bash a Monte Carlo. Nutz.<P>I hate the new Cougars, they will never be what they used to be. I would love an ole "eliminator" Cougar. One of the few cars I would take over a Fiero. Drool.<P>I saw a new Cougar though and it had "eliminator" on the side of it. Did ford come out with a hopped up Cougar "eliminator" edition with a v-8? Just Curious. Even so I still like the old ones much better.||||reg||1
Z||000033||BlackStang95||11-11-2001||03:53 PM||||the new cougars with the v-6 are great cars, especially the xr, limited rear steering, fully independent front and rear suspension, all speed traction control and abs, fwd (no losing the back end) and will beat any stock fiero (0-60 in low 7's.) I heard rumors they were gonna release an svt cougar with over 200 hp, i haven't seen any though.<P>Found some info on the new eliminator cougar for ya kyle, don't try and race it, still a v-6 but 250bhp by way of vortech super charger.<BR> <A HREF="http://supercars.ifn.cx/elim/index.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://supercars.ifn.cx/elim/index.shtml</A> <p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-11-2001).]||||reg||1
