Z||000035||Oreif||11-12-2001||09:14 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>the new cougars with the v-6 are great cars, especially the xr, limited rear steering, fully independent front and rear suspension, all speed traction control and abs, fwd (no losing the back end) and will beat any stock fiero (0-60 in low 7's.) I heard rumors they were gonna release an svt cougar with over 200 hp, i haven't seen any though.<P>Found some info on the new eliminator cougar for ya kyle, don't try and race it, still a v-6 but 250bhp by way of vortech super charger.<BR> <A HREF="http://supercars.ifn.cx/elim/index.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://supercars.ifn.cx/elim/index.shtml</A> <P>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-11-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Road and Track shows the 2002 Cougar as:<BR>0-60 8.2 seconds with auto<BR>0-60 7.8 seconds with manual<BR>2.5L V-6 24-valve with 170HP in a car that weighs<BR>3180 with manual and 3241 with auto trans.<P>Even the website on the eliminator version says the stock 170HP V-6 hit's 0-100kmh (0-62 mph) in 8 seconds. Before one brags, one should get facts first.<P>Bet there are many STOCK Fiero's faster than 7.8 seconds 0-60. Fiero's with stick usually run mid to low 7's (7.2-7.4)<BR>Not bad for a 14-17 year old car. (years that had the V-6)<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
