Z||000037||Ambush||11-12-2001||10:10 AM||||I say Fu** the car. It's not a lamborghini, it's fairly cheap to purchase and pretty easy to restore. Selling the car means something to your parents and you live in thier house. This shouldn't be a hard thought.||||reg||1
Z||000038||pHoOl||11-12-2001||12:33 PM||||I know that you already said that you're giving up the car... but i think it's a wise choice.  I made a mistake when i was nineteen (about a year and a half ago) and trust me, it wouldn't be worth moving out.  I made the decision to stay under a warm roof instead of trying to stand up.  It's not worth it, and now that i looked back on it, i was sooo stupid.  And had i moved out, i'd probably be dead starving by now.  would have really messed up my future<P>moral of the story... stay with the parents.. fieros will still be around in a few years when you're out of the house.  Yeah, they may be slightly more expensive (i'm hoping they appreciate in value), but it's not worth moving out.<P>Good luck with the new car!<P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000039||Mr.Frosty||11-12-2001||02:00 PM||||I moved out,and I've never regretted it.Although,I wasn't in Hot water with the parents either.I don't drop $bills$ like some people on this board,but I can still mod my car out at a slower pace.It also helps that my daily driver is a '96 Ford Ranger that's paid off.  Oops I might have said a bad word<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled<p>[This message has been edited by Mr.Frosty (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000040||BlackStang95||11-12-2001||05:11 PM||||1999   Mercury Cougar              0-60 7.5<P>I thought theyd pick up a few tenths over the years, and they probably did, especially that sweet XR version.  I've never read anything that put any stock fiero under 8 seconds, but oh well.  I'm not gonna turn my friends heartfelt goodbye thread into a flame war, if you wanna debate it further start a new thread.<P>Oh ford rangers are quality! My friends dads 95 is on its original brakes and tires, still has lots of tread and pad nearly 100k miles later.  Built Ford Tough!<p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
