Z||000042||BN Boomer||11-12-2001||06:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Oh ford rangers are quality! My friends dads 95 is on its original brakes and tires, still has lots of tread and pad nearly 100k miles later.  Built Ford Tough!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, that's what I hear alright. Them Ford's come with darn tootin' good tires.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000043||Oreif||11-12-2001||06:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>1999   Mercury Cougar              0-60 7.5<P>I thought theyd pick up a few tenths over the years, and they probably did, especially that sweet XR version.  I've never read anything that put any stock fiero under 8 seconds, but oh well.  I'm not gonna turn my friends heartfelt goodbye thread into a flame war, if you wanna debate it further start a new thread.<P>Oh ford rangers are quality! My friends dads 95 is on its original brakes and tires, still has lots of tread and pad nearly 100k miles later.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> <BR>Built Ford Tough! <P>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-12-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Flame War? All I did was post what was printed in a Road and Track Magazine and on the website link you provided. As for Fiero Spec's Road and Track tested an 85 GT V-6 4-spd and got 0-60 in 7.2 seconds, A few years later the Formula V-6 5-spd was run at 7.4 seconds.<BR>There was no flame's intended. It was just letting everyone know that the new Cougar's are not "faster" than a Fiero. Given the "driver factor" with a manual trans the cars are about equal. The 8 seconds you might mean are auto transmissioned cars which are always slower 0-60 when everything else is equal. The auto's were into the 8 second range just like the Cougar. <P>BTW ~ I thought the "Final Farewell" thread was his "Goodbye Thread"?||||reg||1
